WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.637 --> 00:00:03.640
(upbeat groovy music)

00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:06.450
- Hi again, I'm Linda, and today we're gonna work

00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:09.170
on a pasta installation that has tons

00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:11.207
of different interesting shapes of pasta.

00:00:11.207 --> 00:00:14.760
And we're gonna have so much fun with the pastabilities.

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:16.499
We are going to build out an art piece

00:00:16.499 --> 00:00:18.963
that will have a core, a heart,

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:22.570
and that core in the middle will be made of a raviolone,

00:00:22.570 --> 00:00:25.523
raviolone just means big raviolo.

00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:27.020
So that's our center, that is the center

00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:28.420
of our universe right there.

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:31.543
^Number two is going to be a bunch of square ravioli.

00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:33.840
^With all of this pasta, when we're done today

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:36.630
we are going to boil it all, we're gonna eat

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:38.450
all of these different colors, but sometimes

00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:41.240
there are just pasta scraps that have become too dry.

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:43.470
A couple of uses for them, you can actually bake them,

00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:45.652
turn them into crackers, use them to scoop up

00:00:45.652 --> 00:00:47.371
a cheese or a dip that you've made.

00:00:47.371 --> 00:00:50.458
I feel like pasta and pasta making for me is just

00:00:50.458 --> 00:00:53.682
this zen art that's very meditative.

00:00:53.682 --> 00:00:57.530
We will have triangle ravioli around the squares.

00:00:57.530 --> 00:01:00.050
Those will be orange, they're really funky and pretty.

00:01:00.050 --> 00:01:02.751
^You can't forget the farfalle, farfalle is like

00:01:02.751 --> 00:01:06.063
the classic shape, the little butterflies.

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:07.391
When I was making pasta and I was a little kid

00:01:07.391 --> 00:01:09.871
I could barely hold a knife and we didn't have

00:01:09.871 --> 00:01:13.391
any fancy tools for pasta making so farfalle

00:01:13.391 --> 00:01:15.591
I would say was a really approachable easy one

00:01:15.591 --> 00:01:18.540
to start just because that one is such a classic.

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:21.230
And once you learn to really make it,

00:01:21.230 --> 00:01:22.710
you can make a thousand of them.

00:01:22.710 --> 00:01:25.430
^This is my friend the pasta bike, nice to meet you.

00:01:25.430 --> 00:01:27.000
Next up is a shape called paccheri.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:29.550
Paccheri are rolled on a dowel.

00:01:29.550 --> 00:01:30.991
It's a good thing that we're all adults here

00:01:30.991 --> 00:01:33.270
because it's gonna remind you of something else

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:34.720
but get your mind out of the gutter

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:37.680
and truly just enjoy the artistry of the process.

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:40.030
But I think you can really appreciate and enjoy it

00:01:40.030 --> 00:01:40.990
on many levels.

00:01:40.990 --> 00:01:42.230
^Next up we have culurgiones.

00:01:42.230 --> 00:01:46.260
Culurgiones are from Sardinia, a little island off of Italy.

00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:49.029
It's these little squashy chubby little dumplings

00:01:49.029 --> 00:01:51.132
that are rolled and shaped in a very interesting

00:01:51.132 --> 00:01:52.860
and unique way.

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:55.170
So right now I'm actually really into pasta origami.

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:56.591
I'm getting a lot of inspiration from other

00:01:56.591 --> 00:02:00.050
sort of art forms and how I can bring that to my pasta.

00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:02.100
So for me these shapes are so cool

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:04.610
and I love being able to show people some of the classics

00:02:04.610 --> 00:02:05.863
that we've made today.

00:02:06.010 --> 00:02:07.463
^We have ingannapreti.

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:10.473
Ingannapreti means trick the priest!

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:12.060
What's the story behind that?

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:13.529
And the trick is that they look

00:02:13.529 --> 00:02:15.080
like they're little tortellini

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:17.453
but there's nothing inside, surprise!

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:22.320
We have these really cool just wispy strands of fettuccine.

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:25.927
Our strands are, again, all of the colors represented.

00:02:25.927 --> 00:02:27.840
It actually looks really pretty already,

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:30.400
imagine what it's gonna look like with all the colors!

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:32.110
I always thought my entire life

00:02:32.110 --> 00:02:34.240
that I was an artist and everybody always told me

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:36.360
that I wasn't and that I was terrible.

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:38.729
Well it turns out that I just hadn't found my medium.

00:02:38.729 --> 00:02:41.729
I get really inspired by the entire world around me

00:02:41.729 --> 00:02:43.403
when I'm making pasta.

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:45.955
I feel like when you sort of have found your medium

00:02:45.955 --> 00:02:49.690
you're just always looking for ways to express it

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:51.270
and I do think to me, brings a little bit

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:54.170
of a deeper sense of soul to my work.

00:02:54.170 --> 00:02:56.280
^Pasta la vista, baby.

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:58.203
- [Man] Oh yes!

00:02:59.372 --> 00:03:02.539
(upbeat groovy music)

